# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Prettier writes and verifies LF, so a CRLF checkout makes `npm run format:check`
# fail on the whole tree before it can report a real formatting problem. Without
# this, `core.autocrlf=true` — the default from Git for Windows' installer —
# produces exactly that checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The bundled parity fonts ship in the tree so a clean checkout — and therefore
# a SwiftPM URL dependency — can build GhostteaFonts without running
# `npm run sync:fonts` first. `text=auto` already classifies them as binary by
# content, but say so explicitly: an EOL rewrite here would corrupt a font whose
# bytes are pinned by SHA-256 in native/fonts.lock.json.
*.ttf binary
